    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **33 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp22Tests` bulk-signup checkpoint.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe feature: on owner create, set `bulkSignupWarning` to `true` when more than 80 owners have already been created for that day (by `registrationDate`), otherwise `false`. I followed the existing create-time-assigned-field pattern (like `namesakeCount`), so the value is computed at create and persisted/returned on both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` and `bulkSignupWarningFor(registrationDate)`, which counts existing owners on the (business-day-adjusted) registration date and returns `count > 80`. It's invoked in `addOwner` right after the daily-limit check, reusing the same accumulation path the spec references.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n- **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column is required there.\n\nThe threshold (80) sits below the existing `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT` (100), so owners 81\u2013100 get the warning while still being accepted, and the 101st is still rejected with 429 \u2014 consistent with the existing daily-limit rule.",
